
## 5. "Time adjacency" is not "cause"

### 5.1 Four counterexamples, each observed as a shape rather than argued

| counterexample | naive claim | why it is false | defensible relation | level |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| background task outlives its command | "make modified build/out.o" | the hook fires at command exit; children keep writing for seconds afterwards (`make -j` is the canonical case) | `spawned_by` | Confirmed |
| delayed writeback | "echo modified notes.txt" | `echo x > f` returns after write(2); writeback lands later, so the file event can postdate the process exit | `modified_during` | Weak |
| editor rename-save | "vim modified init.lua" | vim writes a temp file and rename(2)s it over the target; the modified path is the temp path, and the target only appears as a rename destination | `observed_within` | Weak |
| two writers, one file | "cmd-a modified shared.log" | inotify carries no pid (0-E), so a file two processes appended to cannot be attributed to either one | `observed_within` | Unknown |

### 5.2 API constraint: three kinds, no way to spell a cause

| kind string | parses | directional |
|---|---|---|
| `observed_within` | yes | false |
| `spawned_by` | yes | true |
| `modified_during` | yes | false |
| `caused_by` | REJECTED | - |
| `causes` | REJECTED | - |
| `led_to` | REJECTED | - |
| `result_of` | REJECTED | - |

Enforced twice: `RelationKind::parse` returns None, and the schema CHECK in
migrations/0001_init.sql rejects the row. The unit test
`caused_by_is_rejected_by_the_schema` asserts the INSERT fails.

### 5.3 Validation rejects the two illegal shapes

| claim | fork edge | observed input | result |
|---|---|---|---|
| spawned_by with no fork edge | false | true | REJECTED NoForkEvidence |
| Confirmed from inferred inputs only | false | false | REJECTED InferredCannotConfirm |
| modified_during with a real file event | false | true | accepted |
| spawned_by with a kernel fork edge | true | true | accepted |

### 5.4 Rendering is capped by kind, not by level

- `observed_within` at Confirmed -> "cmd:npm test was observed within ./dist/bundle.js's window (Confirmed)" (no causal verb)
- `modified_during` at Confirmed -> "./dist/bundle.js was modified during cmd:npm test's lifetime (Confirmed)" (no causal verb)
- `spawned_by` at Confirmed -> "cmd:npm test was spawned by ./dist/bundle.js (Confirmed)" (no causal verb)

`modified_during` renders "was modified during", never "was modified by", even at
Confirmed. The kind caps the verb; the level only caps confidence in the claim
that is actually being made.

### 5.5 The one relation with a real direction

`spawned_by` is directional because the kernel reported a parent edge at fork
time (`ppid` at the moment the child was created, walked over
/proc/<pid>/stat`). It is still not causation: a parent that spawns `sh -c
"rm -rf build"` did not itself compute anything. It is the *strongest* relation
Phase 0 supports, and it is a containment relation, not a causal one.
